A16_SMSS_72_M016936_039                                                       
                                                                              
Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page C-6                             
                                                                              
These handwritten notes give the data from the postflight calibration         
tests of the Apollo 16 Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP)               
performed at the Lockheed Building in Houston, 2 May 1972.  The page          
gives the loading sequence and the total load in kilograms for eight          
runs.  There are notes at the bottom including "with dirt on index 19"        
and "cleaned on index 21".                                                    
